BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eva Thomas: June Featured Artist in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T170000
UID:260615LoBXogjvsUibWNHhDeplUw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present t
 he art of Eva Thomas in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries in June.  There wil
 l be a reception for the artist on Sunday\, June 14th from 4-7PM.\n\nEva T
 homas is a West Marin based artist studying studio art at San Francisco St
 ate University. She works primarily with ink\, acrylic and spray paint. He
 r art is inspired by the human experience and connection to the natural el
 ements. Eva's work often includes images of faces\, bodies\, and elements 
 from nature. Her goal within her art practice is to connect with the other
 s and make sense of the ever-changing social landscape in which we live. H
 er current work has been focusing on sculptural and multimodal art forms\,
  encapsulating and documenting aspects of her experiences\, observations\,
  and mindsets in college.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/eva-thom
 as-june-featured-artist-in-the-del-mue-galleries
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jan Gross: Between The Veils: Featured June Artist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T170000
UID:260615F8PL23ocZES31S0ERYGuwQ
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present t
 he work of Jan Gross in the West Room of the Maurice Del Mue Galleries in 
 June.  There will be a reception for the artist on June 14th from 4-7 pm.
  \n\n Woodacre artist Jan Gross developed an early connection to the nat
 ural world from her early years in Ontario\, Canada with countless hours s
 pent exploring woods and waterways\, experiences that continue to inform h
 er art. A lifelong painter\, landscape designer\, and dedicated meditation
  practitioner\, she draws inspiration from the dynamic interplay of earth\
 , air\, water\, and fire\, often working in the liminal spaces where one e
 lement meets another. Between the Veils explores love\, loss\, memory\, 
 and transformation through the language of the body. Rich with luminous co
 lor and emotional depth\, Her work reflects her belief in painting as both
  a spiritual practice and a path toward healing.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/jan-gros
 s-june-featured-artist-in-the-del-mue-galleries
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NOAH GALUTEN
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T180000
UID:260614lrEQh79T-EGlCoXqJUbCFg
DESCRIPTION:HEALDSBURG --\n\nWe're excited to welcome chef\, food writer\,
  and James Beard Award-winning cookbook author Noah Galuten to The Burrow 
 in Healdsburg in celebration of his new cookbook\, Grill Time!: Why You S
 hould Be Grilling for Better\, Healthier\, Easier\, and More Delicious Mea
 ls.\n\nJoin Noah and Chef David Baeli for an afternoon of live grilling\, 
 cookbook-inspired fare\, and excellent local wine. Guests may purchase a m
 ixed grilled plate featuring recipes from Grill Time!\, with wines availa
 ble from Right Turn Wine Co.\n\nPurchase a copy of the book at the event a
 nd receive a special discount on your meal.\n\nReservations are recommende
 d - https://www.opentable.com/r/the-burrow-healdsburg\n\nWhether you're a 
 seasoned grill master or simply looking for fresh inspiration for summer c
 ooking\, this is a flavorful opportunity to spend an afternoon with one of
  today's most engaging voices in food.\n\nThursday\, June 18 | 12:00–6:0
 0 PM\n\nThis is a free event. No registration required.\n\nYour new go-to 
 grilling guide\, perfect for newbies and grill masters alike\, from the Ja
 mes Beard Award–winning writer and chef and author of The Don’t Panic
  Pantry Cookbook\n\n“Grill Time! is Noah Galuten’s love letter to the
  magic of live fire—how it makes weeknight cooking easier\, weekend cook
 ing more fun\, and family meals more joyful. With clear techniques and bol
 d\, flexible recipes\, this is grilling built for real life.” —J. Kenj
 i Lopez-Alt\, author of The Wok and The Food Lab\n\nIn Noah Galuten’s 
 backyard\, it’s always grill time! With two young children\, Galuten kno
 ws firsthand how important it is to get flavorful\, healthy food on the ta
 ble quickly and easily. His secret: the grill\, which allows easily custom
 izable dinners for all different palates. In Grill Time! Galuten embraces 
 his love of bright flavors\, comfort foods\, and veggie-forward dishes to 
 create meals that work for backyard barbecues\, pool parties\, camping tri
 ps\, and\, of course\, quick weeknight dinners.\n\nHere are delicious opti
 ons for meat eaters\, vegetarians\, and vegans alike:\n\n\\*THE BEST BURGE
 RS AND SANDWCHES! From Backyard Bacon Cheeseburgers\, the Juiciest Turkey 
 Burgers\, and Pork Souvlaki Pitas to a Tofu Bánh Mì with Lemongrass BBQ 
 Sauce and a Smoky Grilled Caprese Sandwich\, there’s something for every
 one.\n\n\\*VEGGIE SIDES AND MAINS GALORE: Grilled Asparagus and Wilted Whi
 te Cheddar\, Perfect Grilled Potatoes\, Miso-Butter Corn\, Stuffed Poblano
 s with Cilantro-Lime Tahini\, a Grilled Veggie Burrito like no other\, and
  so much more.\n\n\\*BIG SALADS! A Southwest Veggie Chop\, a Spicy Grilled
  Chicken Caesar with Garlic Bread Croutons\, and a Grilled Shrimp Niçoise
 \, to name just a few.\n\n\\*FISH AND SEAFOOD: From Grilled Clams with Coc
 ktail Butter to Grilled Fish Tacos with Chile Crunch and Smoke-Grilled Mis
 o Black Cod.\n\n\\*CHICKEN\, BEEF\, AND PORK\, every which way: Achiote-Li
 me Chicken Breast and Pickle-Brined Drumsticks with Spicy Honey\; a Tavern
 a Steak for weeknights and a Smoke-Grilled Bone-In Rib Eye for weekends\; 
 a Buttermilk-Brined Pork Chop with Grilled Lemon and Smoke-Grilled Baby Ba
 cks.\n\nThere’s also a special guide to the ultimate Hermosillo-Style Ca
 rne Asada. And for any newbies on the grill\, or pros who want to expand t
 heir grill knowledge\, Grill Time! is a helpful guide on grill mechanics
 \, including the differences between smokers\, gas grills\, and charcoal g
 rills and the cooking techniques that go along with each one. Level up you
 r grilling game with Grill Time!\n\nAuthor: Noah Galuten is a chef\, James
  Beard Award-winning cookbook author and author of The Don’t Panic Pant
 ry Cookbook. He is also the co-author of On Vegetables: Modern Recipes fo
 r the Home Kitchen with Jeremy Fox\, and Bludso's BBQ Cookbook: A Family
  Affair in Smoke and Soul with Kevin Bludso\, among other titles. He curre
 ntly lives in Los Angeles with his wife\, children and small dog.
LOCATION:The Burrow
URL:https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-06-18/noah-galuten
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
