BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laurin Hunter & Jolene Dixon & Paula Fong
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T000000
UID:260608DsA32k5CHUSPLDTLfU2EVA
DESCRIPTION:Laurin Hunter is an independent San Francisco Bay Area based s
 inger/songwriter interweaving elements of folk\, americana\, rock\, pop\, 
 alternative\, and world music. Laurin is an artist who joyfully defies lim
 itations and his explosive live shows leave audience members feeling trans
 ported\, rejuvenated and understood. His utilization of alternate tunings\
 , tastefully innovative guitar work\, soulful vocal delivery \\(spanning f
 our octaves\\)\, and introspective lyrical storytelling combine to take li
 steners on a transformational journey of discovery they’ve never been on
  before. \n\nAfter surviving a near fatal car accident while studying econ
 omics at Sonoma State University\, Laurin’s perspective and life traject
 ory drastically changed\, catapulting him to dedicate his new lease on lif
 e to his musical artistry. Shortly afterwards\, Laurin attended Belmont Un
 iversity in Nashville\, TN where he studied and mentored with Grammy Award
  winning songwriters. He has since won competitions such as the West Coast
  Songwriters contest and NSAI new song competition. He has toured across t
 he US and played venues such as the Freight and Salvage in Berkeley\, CA a
 s well as the Blue Bird Cafe ASCAP Writer Showcase in Nashville\, TN. Laur
 in's 2023 self released album “Face Up” has accumulated over 4 million
  global streams\, and he's racked up millions more writing for other major
  label artists. \n\nLaurin’s upcoming release “The Ontario Sessions”
  is both a short film and EP where Laurin documents his time in Algonquin 
 National Park while grappling with the recent loss of his father. During t
 he film\, Laurin performs covers of iconic Canadian artists such as Joni M
 itchell and Neil Young while also showcasing original music he composed in
  the park. \n\nThroughout the entirety of his career\, Laurin has cultivat
 ed a vast\, supportive international audience that continues to grow by th
 e day. Ultimately\, he hopes to captivate\, heal\, and inspire his listene
 rs with heartfelt music.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1038805157?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
