BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Draw Like An Imagineer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T120000
UID:260618xTAAGgZIZUOH-i84sWRxSg
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nEnter into a playful\, behind-the-scenes drawing worksho
 p inspired by real-world Walt Disney Imagineering techniques\, led by arti
 st and former Imagineer Maggie Parr. Through fun\, guided exercises\, you'
 ll explore how storytelling and drawing come together to build imaginative
  worlds&mdash\;learning to sketch from your imagination\, think in three d
 imensions\, and bring ideas to life with creative problem-solving. Blendin
 g professional insight with a relaxed\, inspiring atmosphere\, this worksh
 op invites artists and curious creatives of all levels to experiment\, pla
 y\, and discover new ways of seeing\, thinking\, and creating.\n\nThis wor
 kshop is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nMaggie Parr 
 began her career at Walt Disney Imagineering\, working as a show designer 
 on attractions for Toontown and Animal Kingdom. After leaving Disney to fo
 cus on painting\, she continued as an independent contractor while expandi
 ng into book illustration\, murals\, portraits\, comics\, and television w
 riting. She trained in classical painting with artists including Steve Hus
 ton\, Cheryl Kline\, Steven Assael\, Jeremy Lipking\, and Joseph Q. Daily\
 , later earning an MFA. She now teaches students of all levels while maint
 aining an active painting practice.\n\nLearn More: \n\nwww.maggieparr.comw
 ww.parrcreate.com@maggieparrart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-draw-like-an-i
 magineer?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Making Sense of AI: A Conversation for Artists and Makers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260618f9ovV9fPJEGWBV4KopGzOA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nGenerative AI is changing how
  art gets made\, and it's bringing a lot of hype\, worry\, and mixed feeli
 ngs with it. In this session\, Daniel Shiplacoff opens up an honest conver
 sation about what's actually going on and what it means for the people mak
 ing things. We'll talk about how these tools work\, where the tricky quest
 ions sit around training data and authorship\, how AI might fit into a wor
 king practice without taking over the parts that matter most\, and how to 
 talk about all of it plainly with clients\, galleries\, and the people aro
 und you. Whether you work on a screen or at a bench\, the goal is to leave
  with better questions and a clearer sense of your own voice.\n\nThis clas
 s is located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: Daniel Shiplacoff 
 is a product and system designer. He helped pioneer the gestural interacti
 on model now common on smartphones\, with work on Palm webOS\, Android\, a
 nd Material Design at Google. More recently he co-founded Hello Wonder\, a
 n AI browser for kids where each family's values shape the experience. The
 se days he's building and writing about personal AI &mdash\; systems that 
 run on your own machine\, and answer to identity\, agency\, and privacy.\n
 \nLearn more about Dan:\n\nwww.danship.com\n\n@danship
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-conversation-ab
 out-ai-daniel-shiplacoff?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Going Global: Opportunities for the International Artist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T120000
UID:260618eTqrnFzxR02-C8DGa2e11w
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nExpand your art practice beyo
 nd borders in this focused\, career-building workshop led by a Santa Rosa&
 ndash\;based artist\, curator\, writer\, former college instructor\, and F
 ulbright Scholar. Designed for artists ready to engage with the global art
  world\, this class explores how to access international residencies\, gra
 nts\, exhibitions\, and collaborations. You'll learn how to craft compelli
 ng proposals\, navigate cross-cultural applications\, and position your wo
 rk for opportunities abroad. With practical strategies and insider insight
 \, you'll leave with the confidence and tools to take your practice onto a
 n international stage.  \n\nThis class is located in the Main Gallery.\n\n
 About the Teacher: \n\nJane Ingram Allen is an internationally recognized 
 artist\, curator\, and writer specializing in hand papermaking and ecoart.
  Originally from Alabama and now based in Santa Rosa\, California\, she ha
 s taught widely across the U.S. and abroad\, and has led workshops in coun
 tries throughout Asia and beyond. Her work has been featured in global exh
 ibitions\, and she regularly writes for publications such as Sculpture and
  Fiber Art Now. A recipient of numerous international residencies and awar
 ds&mdash\;including multiple Fulbright grants&mdash\;Allen continues to ex
 hibit and contribute to the global art community. \n\nLearn more about Jan
 e:\n\nwww.janeingramallen.comhttp://www.janeingramallen.com/residency/resi
 dency.htmhttps://janeingramallen.wordpress.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-going-global-op
 portunities?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
