SUMMARY:Jan Gross: Between The Veils: Featured June Artist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T170000
UID:260615lm3L18WWVkq8vR4OPkw8xw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present t
 he work of Jan Gross in the West Room of the Maurice Del Mue Galleries in 
 June.  There will be a reception for the artist on June 14th from 4-7 pm.
  \n\n Woodacre artist Jan Gross developed an early connection to the nat
 ural world from her early years in Ontario\, Canada with countless hours s
 pent exploring woods and waterways\, experiences that continue to inform h
 er art. A lifelong painter\, landscape designer\, and dedicated meditation
  practitioner\, she draws inspiration from the dynamic interplay of earth\
 , air\, water\, and fire\, often working in the liminal spaces where one e
 lement meets another. Between the Veils explores love\, loss\, memory\, 
 and transformation through the language of the body. Rich with luminous co
 lor and emotional depth\, Her work reflects her belief in painting as both
  a spiritual practice and a path toward healing.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/jan-gros
 s-june-featured-artist-in-the-del-mue-galleries
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eva Thomas: June Featured Artist in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T170000
UID:260615OPbplmrYTk-TbtcdpAd95w
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present t
 he art of Eva Thomas in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries in June.  There wil
 l be a reception for the artist on Sunday\, June 14th from 4-7PM.\n\nEva T
 homas is a West Marin based artist studying studio art at San Francisco St
 ate University. She works primarily with ink\, acrylic and spray paint. He
 r art is inspired by the human experience and connection to the natural el
 ements. Eva's work often includes images of faces\, bodies\, and elements 
 from nature. Her goal within her art practice is to connect with the other
 s and make sense of the ever-changing social landscape in which we live. H
 er current work has been focusing on sculptural and multimodal art forms\,
  encapsulating and documenting aspects of her experiences\, observations\,
  and mindsets in college.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/eva-thom
 as-june-featured-artist-in-the-del-mue-galleries
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
