BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flynn Creek Circus - The Cricket and the Wren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T200000
UID:2605297P6o_AFPbEOhrRncwJe6NA
DESCRIPTION:Flynn Creek Circus Presents ‘The Cricket & the Wren’: a hi
 ghly original\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acroba
 tics and athletically stunning skill. Sponsored by the City of Rohnert Par
 k.\n\n**Rohnert Park\, CA— June 18 - June 28**– This 2026 season\, Fly
 nn Creek Circus invites audiences to ‘*The Cricket & the Wren’* — me
 morable family fun and Artful athleticism under the circus big top.\n\nA m
 erchant’s daughter sets out to find the castle where the horizon meets t
 he sea. In order to  break the spell of the Frog Prince\, she must brave 
 a harrowing journey filled with wonder.\n\nAlong the adventure\, she encou
 nters Jack and the Beanstalk’s sassy cow\, an out of pocket Pirate and t
 he secret sacrifice of the cricket and the wren. \n\nFeaturing aerialists
 \, jugglers\, knife throwers\, and laugh out loud comedy\, this circus ble
 nds classic storybook archetypes with imaginative new heroes. **The Cricke
 t and the Wren** will surprise\, dazzle and delight all ages. \n\nIn addi
 tion to the family friendly showings\,  and the interactive children's ca
 mp program held under the circus big top\,  Flynn Creek Circus also prese
 nts the wildly popular 'Adults Only Show' boasting outrageous acts\, dark 
 comedy\, and an infamous party atmosphere. Check the website for select ad
 ults only showtimes as well as special discount nights.\n\nSpectators for 
 all showings are invited to the tent to experience the magic up to 30 minu
 tes before each show. The event will offer beer\, wine\, and light concess
 ion for purchase and include a 15 minute intermission during the two hour 
 show.\n\n**Limited free parking** is available at 500 City Center Drive. P
 atrons should then cross the street in the pedestrian crossing at the Rohn
 ert Park Expressway and State Farm Drive traffic signal.\n\nTickets for Fl
 ynn Creek Circus are now available for purchase online at flynncreekcircus
 .com. Individual ticket prices start at $27 or\, for table reservations\, 
 options start at $98 for two attendees. \n\nFind showtimes and more detai
 ls on the camp programs for ages 5-8 and 7-15 at flynncreekcircus.com\n\nE
 arly booking is encouraged for this highly anticipated event. \n\n**Locat
 ion:** *SE corner lot at Rohnert Park Expressway and State Farm Dr. Rohner
 t Park\, CA 94928* *Under the circus big top*\n\nFor more information\, pr
 ess inquiries\, or interview requests\, please contact Stella Perry at mar
 keting@flynncreekcircus.com. High-resolution images and media resources ar
 e also available upon request\n\n**About Flynn Creek Circus:**Flynn Creek 
 Circus is an original\, modern circus company touring across the Pacific N
 orthwest\, delighting audiences with world-class acrobatics\, storytelling
 \, and comedy. Known for its innovative productions and intimate tent show
 s\, the company redefines the traditional circus experience
LOCATION:Under the circus big top
URL:https://flynncreekcircus.ticketspice.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T170000
UID:2605297D3ze5lGkE2iBj6zTa1g2g
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T180000
UID:260515CVmil_3z8ESZQDt1aLqBBA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
