BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Luminous Landscape: Mastering the "Wipeout" Underpainting and 
 Oil Glazing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T160000
UID:260610RUREzgN2E0GHMhGOPph-JA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nIn this workshop\, you move beyond simple shapes and exp
 lore how to infuse your work with mood and atmosphere. You will learn how 
 to build a composition from the ground up\, starting with a classic wipeou
 t technique to establish values before moving into the vibrant world of ac
 rylics.\n\nWhat You Will Learn:\n\nThe Foundation of Light: Master the "wi
 peout" method to create a roadmap for your painting. Color Mixing &amp\; H
 armony: Learn to blend pigments to create realistic skies\, rolling hills\
 , and textured foliage.The Painterly Approach: Move away from stiff lines 
 and embrace fluid\, expressive brushwork that breathes life into your canv
 as. Compositional Secrets: Understand how to guide the viewer's eye throug
 h a landscape using classic Hudson River School principles.This workshop i
 s located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nNorthern California&
 ndash\;based artist Roberto Miliano creates atmospheric landscapes that br
 idge 19th-century tradition with contemporary vibrancy. Inspired by the To
 nalist and Hudson River School movements\, his work captures the mood of t
 he natural world&mdash\;from the foggy Pacific coast to quiet mountain wat
 ers. His process begins with intuitive sketching\, followed by acrylic und
 erpainting and layered oils that build rich\, dreamlike depth. Blending cl
 assical palettes with modern materials\, his paintings evoke both nostalgi
 a and a sense of quiet mystery.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-wipeout-oil-gl
 azing?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
