DESCRIPTION:**Learn-to-Row Summer Camp Information - North Bay Rowing Club
 **\n\nAt the **Learn-to-Row** **Summer Camp**\, athletes will learn the 
 fundamentals of the sport both on land and on the water. They will meet cu
 rrent members of the team who will help guide and instruct them in proper 
 form\, and learn what it means to be a part of a team. Athletes will begin
  instruction on-land learning proper boat handling and basic sculling tech
 nique\, and then they will practice their skills on-water in singles and t
 eam boats that holds either 2 or 4 students in a shell. Students may have 
 the opportunity to learn more about racing skills and perform short distan
 ce races at the end of the week-long session.\n\nSummer camps are open to
  ***all*** rowers\, whether you're a looking to explore a new sport or s
 imply looking for a fun activity! No experience is required!\n\n**Athletes
 **: 13-17 years\n\n**Prerequisite:** No experience is required!!\n\n**Sess
 ion Days:** Monday through Friday\n\n**Session Times :** 9:00am -12:00pm
 \n\n**Learn To Row Session Dates:** Session 1: June 22 - 26 Session 2: Jul
 y 6 - 10 Session 3: July 13 - 17 Session 4: July 20 - 24 Session 5: July 2
 7 - 31
LOCATION:North Bay Rowing Club
URL:https://www.northbayrowing.org/2026-summer-camps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
