BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Connection: From Found Objects to Meaningful Assemblage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T120000
UID:260618hQqIrk_9p0GKj0AkOKNQDQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nThis hands-on workshop teaches students to transform fou
 nd objects into meaningful mixed media assemblages by exploring intuitive 
 storytelling and metaphorical connections between materials. Moving beyond
  traditional art methods\, participants create narrative-driven pieces usi
 ng curated vintage and natural objects\, leaving with both a finished artw
 ork and a fresh perspective on creative possibilities.\n\nThis workshop is
  located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nAnne Monk brings a d
 istinctive blend of science and art to her work\, combining the precision 
 of a Master Science Educator with a lifelong creative practice rooted in f
 ine arts. Raised in a professional artist's studio\, she has explored jewe
 lry design\, painting\, printmaking\, and photography alongside a distingu
 ished career that includes leadership and educational roles at Marine Worl
 d Africa USA\, the Katherine Delmar Burke School\, and institutions such a
 s the California Academy of Sciences\, Audubon Canyon Ranch\, and UC Berke
 ley. Her assemblages reflect this rich intersection&mdash\;merging scienti
 fic insight\, structural design\, and intuitive artistic expression.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/the-art-of-connection-from
 -found-objects?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Lanterns
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T160000
UID:2606186JcnqcivQkKgizhUAY_x9w
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nTransform simple paper lanterns into glowing works of ar
 t using the magical process of cyanotype. In this hands-on workshop\, you'
 ll explore how light\, chemistry\, and layered imagery come together to cr
 eate luminous blue prints directly on cyanotype-coated lanterns. Experimen
 t with botanicals\, photographic and hand-drawn images on transparencies\,
  and mulberry paper patches to craft a one-of-a-kind\, functional work of 
 art. Learn how to expand your knowledge of cyanotype chemistry and light-b
 ased printmaking while discovering creative ways to compose imagery on a t
 hree-dimensional surface. Leave with a beautifully handcrafted lantern tha
 t glows with your own unique design.\n\nThis workshop is located in the cl
 assroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nAsh Hay is a multidisciplinary artist 
 based in Santa Rosa\, California\, whose work and teaching are rooted in c
 uriosity\, experimentation\, and community. They serve as Printshop Lab Te
 chnician at Santa Rosa Junior College and founded the Sonoma County Sketch
 book Club\, creating spaces for artists to connect and grow. Ash holds a B
 FA from Sonoma State University and was honored with the Creative Sonoma D
 iscovered Emerging Artist Award. Their work has been exhibited at the Sono
 ma County Museum\, the Contemporary Jewish Museum in San Francisco\, and N
 eon Raspberry Art House in Occidental. With over a decade of experience as
  a teaching artist\, Ash brings a playful\, exploratory spirit&mdash\;grou
 nded in strong technical skill&mdash\;to every class and workshop they lea
 d.\n\nTo learn more about Ash: www.ashhay.comAnd on Instagram: @ashhayart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-cyanotype-lant
 erns?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All Access Pass for 2026 PAC Academy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T210000
UID:260610bXfAtBXKdUimJabE3JrFpA
DESCRIPTION:Get 26 workshops\, virtual classes or lectures with your pass.
   Once you complete your purchase\, your code will appear to redeem a clas
