BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Botanical Watercolor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T120000
UID:260618W0Dn5cS8mEq3dMVjmMcXJQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nIn this relaxed and inspiring two-hour workshop\, immers
 e yourself in the beauty of botanical watercolor as you paint directly fro
 m real leaves\, flowers\, and natural forms. Guided by observation\, you'l
 l learn simple\, approachable techniques for capturing organic shapes\, lu
 minous color\, and the subtle movement of nature. Inspired by contemporary
  botanical artists\, this class invites you to loosen up\, experiment free
 ly\, and rediscover the pleasure of truly seeing the natural world. Perfec
 t for all levels\, this welcoming experience includes all materials&mdash\
 ;no prior watercolor experience needed.\n\nThis workshop is located in the
  classroom.PAC Provides:Watercolor\, paper\, palettes\, brushes\, cups\, p
 aper towelsTeacher Provides:Flowers\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nBorn and rai
 sed in Mill Valley\, California\, Genevieve Elkin is a multidisciplinary a
 rtist now based in Petaluma. She earned a BFA in Illustration from Parsons
  School of Design and has professionally managed art departments\, support
 ing artists and new media on high-profile projects. Genevieve loves painti
 ng\, drawing\, and exploring ceramics\, and enjoys helping students experi
 ment\, have fun\, and develop their own creative voice.\n\nTo learn more:@
 gennaelkin
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-botanical-wate
 rcolor?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma Landscapes: Drawing Nature\, Mapping Memory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T160000
UID:2606131z6zfYHq4UiSSZrignupdQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nImmerse yourself in the landscapes of Petaluma and trans
 form your observations into expressive illustrations. This workshop blends
  outdoor exploration with in-studio practice\, inviting you to absorb the 
 textures\, light\, and atmosphere of the natural world and translate that 
 experience through drawing and watercolor. Using techniques like memory ma
 pping\, landscape sketching\, and visual journaling\, you'll develop a per
 sonal language for capturing place and wonder. With a balance of independe
 nt outdoor study and guided studio work\, this class is perfect for artist
 s looking to deepen both their observation skills and creative response to
  nature.\n\nThis class is located offsite. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nDani
 elle Bronson is a Bay Area&ndash\;based artist\, researcher\, and graphic 
 designer whose multidisciplinary practice bridges visual art\, critical th
 eory\, and digital media. She holds a BA in Studio Art and Art History fro
 m the University of California\, Davis and works across collage\, web-base
 d projects\, and research-driven work that explores themes of language\, p
 erception\, and contemporary culture. In addition to her creative practice
 \, she has worked as an educator\, arts administrator\, and designer\, con
 tributing to organizations such as Southern Exposure and Verge Center for 
 the Arts. Her work reflects an interest in experimentation\, translation\,
  and the evolving relationship between technology\, meaning\, and human ex
 perience.\n\nLearn more about Danielle: \n\nwww.intertidal.studio.com\n\n@
 intertidalstudio
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-drawing-nature?
 aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
