BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Marcus & Devin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T143000
UID:260608weXQtjh2uEOxkXJwmVgdIA
DESCRIPTION:Soul Meets Keys: Marcus & Devin Live\n\nJoin us for No Cell Su
 ndays with Marcus & Devin\, a duo that transforms Sunday afternoons into s
 omething extraordinary.\n\nMarcus Urani is one of Northern California's mo
 st celebrated pianists and keyboardists. Educated in musical theory and an
  original member of Groundation\, Marcus has toured the world and spent 25
 \\+ years composing\, arranging\, producing\, and playing with countless m
 usical acts. With mastery across nearly all genres\, Marcus creates rich m
 usical landscapes that captivate from the first note.\n\nPaired with vocal
 ist and lyricist Devin Ruddick's emotive and soaring vocals\, this duo del
 ivers a one-two punch that captivates without intrusion—adding melodic b
 liss as they cover a catalog of meaningful artists spanning seven decades.
 \n\nWhat's No Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\,
  reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Check
  your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Bring
  a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to 
 be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-marcus-devin
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Abstraction in Mixed Media: Learn to Develop a Powerful Abstract P
 ainting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T150000
UID:2606078YnLunFUWU2DiXXHbLYK-g
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, June 28\, 2026 10:00 AM – 3:00 PM\n\nLo
 cation\n\nGallery 212\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categorie
 s: Drawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistr
 ation Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$20\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n
 \n$120\n\nCreate a compelling abstract piece: explore intuition\, layering
 \, balance\, focal points\, and mixed media techniques with bold\, experim
 ental tools.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nThis workshop guides you through the fu
 ll journey of creating a compelling abstract work from start to finish. Yo
 u’ll strengthen your artistic instincts while learning how to build a me
 aningful concept or visual narrative that anchors your piece. We will expl
 ore:\n\nDeveloping intuitive decision-making\n\nBuilding\, adjusting\, and
  refining layers\n\nFinding balance between control and spontaneity\n\nCre
 ating dynamic focal points and luminous highlights\n\nUsing a wide range o
 f mixed media materials — including collage\, paint\, crayons\, oil past
 els\, and unexpected household tools like plastic wrap and Q-tips — you
 ’ll experiment with texture\, mark-making\, and innovative surface techn
 iques. This class is about courage\, curiosity\, and learning how to “wr
 estle” with a painting until it becomes something honest\, layered\, and
  alive. Paints and substrate will be provided through the materials fee. S
 ee the supply list for additional items to bring. Note: There will be a on
 e-hour lunch break. Please bring a bag lunch.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/abstraction-in-mixed-media-
 learn-to-develop-a-powerful-abstract-painting/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - School Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T113000
UID:260606KsR14tQaZUuEJS3EgqhGtg
DESCRIPTION:Teachers\, Text Books and School Spirit\n\nSteve Deas\n\nSchoo
 ls have long been institutions of key importance in Healdsburg. Steve Deas
  will look at the early days of education\, when farm kids got their basic
  education in one-room country school houses and the Seventh Day Adventist
  community established a college that sat near the center of town. Then he
 ’ll talk about more modern schools and their importance in the community
 . And we’ll ask the audience to share stories of favorite teachers\, cla
 ssroom hijinks and school Spirit.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
