BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temp.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T220000
UID:260330pb8t5LXh_EiqJLpwUzwR5A
DESCRIPTION:Ain’t Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical 
 that follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets of 
 Detroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance m
 oves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the
  music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success the
 y achieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and 
 political tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in A
 merica.\n\nThis thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betray
 al is set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Gi
 rl\,” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rollin
 g Stone” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Domi
 nique Morisseau \\(Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams
 ’s 1988 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty clos
 e to perfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling 
 and Electrifying.”\n\nAin’t Too Proud is presented through special ar
 rangement with Music Theatre International \\(MTI\\). All authorized perfo
 rmance materials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com\n\nMusic Thea
 tre International gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Tempt
 ations a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the
  history of The Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/broadway-under-the-star
 s-ain-t-too-proud-the-life-and-times-of-the-temp/18460828/2026-06-28T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monica Da Silva
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T000000
UID:260327uEW6mT7-ck2mYoh--rySfw
DESCRIPTION:Monica da Silva grew up living between The United States and B
 elém\, Brazil\, a city on the Amazon River. A love of travel and foreign 
 language helped to forge her unique sound. \n\n \n\nParalleling her life\,
  da Silva's music contains an eclectic mix of Brazilian and American influ
 ences. Her sound can be classified as International Fusion\, as it is heav
 ily influenced by Brazilian music\, namely Bossa Nova\, but also incorpora
 tes elements of Lounge\, Electronica\, Indie Pop\, and Worldbeat. Da Silva
  brings her cultural diversity to her songs\, smoothly flowing between Eng
 lish\, Portuguese\, and Spanish.\n\n \n\nIn 2010\, da Silva released her a
 lbum "Brasilissima" . The record featured songs in both of her native lang
 uages - English and Portuguese. The first single "Aí Então"\, “was cho
 sen by Putumayo World Music to be included on their compilation “Brazili
 an Beat”. The upbeat\, psychedelic track "That's Not The Way" was chosen
  by the music director of ESPN to be played during the programming of The 
 FIFA World Cup in 2014\, alongside major recording artists Coldplay\, Sér
 gio Mendes\, Pitbull\, Jennifer Lopez\, The Black Eyed Peas\, Stan Getz\, 
 and Astrud Gilberto. \n\nDa Silva's single "Soldado de Amor" \\(2017\\) ha
 s been featured in the BBC One series "The Replacement”\, in the Paramou
 nt Network series "American Woman"\, and in a 2019 campaign for the design
 er Tory Burch.\n\nHer music has also been featured in the series "Heartlan
 d"\, and in an ad for Patron Tequila. She is currently recording a new\, f
 ull-length solo album\, as well as writing and recording with her project\
 , Complicated Animals.
LOCATION:Napa River Inn
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107954604?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
