BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Studio to Street: The Art of Capturing People
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T120000
UID:260618urpVCVk_OUKrhDxIEmyU5Q
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nIn this practical\, skill-building workshop\, photograph
 er Tom Chown introduces students to the fundamentals of creating compellin
 g photo portraits in both studio and on-location settings. Participants wi
 ll learn how to work with light\, compose strong images\, and connect with
  their subjects to capture authentic expression. The class explores key di
 fferences between controlled studio environments and dynamic outdoor or re
 al-world locations\, giving students the confidence to adapt their approac
 h in any setting. Designed for beginners and emerging photographers\, this
  workshop provides a solid foundation for anyone looking to create engagin
 g\, professional-quality portraits.\n\nBring your digital camera!\n\nThis 
 workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nTom Chown 
 is a Bay Area photographer whose work spans weddings\, theater\, and fine 
 art. Recognized by CBS San Francisco as one of the top photography studios
  in the North Bay\, he travels throughout the region and offers services f
 or destination weddings. His photography has been featured in publications
  including San Francisco Magazine\, Wedding Channel\, Napa Wedding Source\
 , and Napa Appellation. He has also documented over 60 stage productions f
 or the Summer Repertory Theatre at Santa Rosa Junior College\, and his fin
 e art images have appeared in Artweek\, West Art\, High Performance Magazi
 ne\, and the Press Democrat.\n\nLearn more about Tom:\n\nwww.tomchownphoto
 .com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-studio-to-stree
 t?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art in Action: Transforming Public Space
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T010000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T160000
UID:260618snjbzofXsEWo-OYxPO7Fdg
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nStep beyond the studio and into the city in this bold\, 
 interactive workshop exploring how art can spark connection and transform 
 public space. You'll dive into the history of socially engaged art\, then 
 dream up your own creative interventions to address issues like isolation\
 , disconnection\, and screen fatigue. You will prototype your project usin
 g simple materials\, and then stage it temporarily in a public space. Thro
 ugh collaborative brainstorming\, rapid prototyping\, and real-world insta
 llation\, you'll bring your ideas to life&mdash\;inviting strangers to sha
 re stories\, slow down\, and engage in meaningful ways. Along the way\, yo
 u'll break through creative blocks\, build community\, and learn how to me
 asure impact and grow your projects from temporary experiments into lastin
 g\, city-shaping experiences.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom
 . \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nHunter Franks is an artist whose work centers
  on creating opportunities for connection\, storytelling\, and reimagining
  social norms through community-based public art\, writing\, and installat
 ion. His projects&mdash\;ranging from a 500-person dinner on a freeway to 
 global initiatives like the Neighborhood Postcard Project&mdash\;invite pe
 ople to share experiences and recognize their common humanity. Founder of 
 the League of Creative Interventionists\, his work has been presented at v
 enues including the de Young Museum and featured in major publications suc
 h as The Guardian and Los Angeles Times. A recipient of honors including t
 he Knight Cities Challenge and a Yerba Buena Center for the Arts Fellowshi
 p\, Franks lives in Northern California and speaks nationally about art's 
 role in fostering empathy\, equity\, and civic imagination.\n\nLearn more 
 about Hunter: hunterfranks.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-transforming-pu
 blic-space?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
