BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Marin County Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T230000
UID:2606171gkRGxMNXU-MLiGacSWYMQ
DESCRIPTION:Price: Five-Day Fun Pass $85\, Any Day Ticket $30\n\nTicket In
 fo: https://tickets.marincenter.org/eventperformances.asp?evt=457\n\nLink:
  https://marinfair.org/\n\nStars\, Stripes and Stories\n\nJul y 1 - 5\n\n1
 1am-11pm\n\nNo entry after 10pm.\n\nThe Ma rin County Fair is a one price 
 gate. All prices include all live entertainment\, including headline conce
 rts on the Island Stage\\*\, 28 carnival rides\, spectacular nightly firew
 orks\, and exciting exhibits and experi ences you can only find at the Mar
 in County Fair.\n\n\\* Access to the Island Tent begins at 6pm each night 
 and at 2pm on July 4 . The Island may be closed if capacity is reached\, b
 ut additional concert viewing is available on the adjacent Special Events 
 Lawn. All access is on a first-come\, first-served basis for seating and s
 tan ding room on the Island.\n\nBuy a Five-Day Fun Pass and save! Makes a 
 great holiday gift!\n\nFrom November 28 through April 30\, the only way to
  secure discounted tickets to the Marin County Fair is to purchase a Five-
 Day Fun Pass. The Pass provides admission t o all five days of the Fair fo
 r only $85 \\(a 35% discount\\) plus you will receive a Marin County Fair 
 clear tote bag.\n\nBeginning Novem ber 28 and through the Fair\, you can p
 urchase an Any Day Ticket\, granting you admission to the Fair any single 
 day of your choice including July 4 for $30.\n\nIf you are looking for dis
 counted tickets\, we have two great options:\n\n• From November 28 throu
 gh April 30 \, you can purchase a Five-Day Fun Pass for just $85 \\(a disc
 ount of over 35%\\)\n\n• From May 1 through June 30\, you can purchase a
  Select Day Ticket for any specified day\, other than July 4\, for just $2
 0\n\nS pecial Admissions\n\nWednesday\, July 1\n\nAges 12 and under FREE\n
 \nAges 65 and over FREE\n\nVeterans with ID FREE\n\nDaily\n\nChildren 3 an
 d under FREE\n\nActive-duty military FREE\n\nAll tickets are final sale. N
 o refunds or exchanges.\n\nTicket policies: All Fair tickets may be purcha
 sed online 24/7. Tickets may also be purchased at the Marin Center Box Off
 ice when open for other events. Tickets are valid only on the day\\(s\\) f
 or which they were issued and cannot be exchanged for an alternate day or 
 refunded. There are NO ticketing kiosks at the gates\; a QR code to purcha
 se tickets will be posted at all entry points. All Fair tickets include ge
 neral admission to the headline concerts on a first-come\, first-served ba
 sis. All ticket sales are final. No refunds or exchanges.
LOCATION:Fairgrounds
URL:https://marinfair.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Local Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T180000
UID:260616lRkvjCQ5vkeeuPNvVJqPuw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  6/15/26\n\n**JULY EXHIBIT: LOC
 AL COLOR**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 29 – July 26\, 2026**\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, July 4\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Linda Barretta  
 and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  
 Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beaut
 iful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Linda Barretta** presents **Local Color\,** a collecti
 on unveiling new oil paintings that tap into the vivid natural hues found 
 in our region’s breathtaking beauty.  From flowers to vineyards\, colo
 r takes a starring role in these works.  The deep purple hills in “Sun
 flower Daze” intensify the golden sweep of the sunflowers.  A peach tr
 ee celebrates the season with a glorious pink floral display in “Spring 
 Blooms.”  In “Winery Farm and Gardens\,” framed through a natural 
 arch of trees\, a sunlit vineyard draws the viewer.  “We are so fortun
 ate to live in Sonoma wine country – it’s stunning beauty is a daily i
 nspiration to pick up my brushes and paint\,” commented Barretta. \n\nL
 iving in Healdsburg\, Sonoma wine country is Barretta’s homebase.  She
  developed her impressionist style and skills through numerous hours of pl
 ein air painting and studying with master artists.  When Barretta create
 s the composition\, she is observing the play of light and colors that wil
 l highlight the compelling quality of the scene.  Her aim is to translat
 e her inspiration to the viewer.  From the rough sketch to the final bru
 shstroke\, this is the task she loves.  Barretta participates in the Art
  Trails Open Studio program and her works are exhibited regionally and thr
 oughout the country\,\n\nMeet the artist: Barretta will host the Gallery o
 n July 4\, 6 & 26\, 2:30 – 6pm and July 22\, 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\nThe Sta
 irway Smallworks Showcase features **Beverly Bird’s Birds by Bird\,** a
  collection of acrylic paintings that depict our feathered friends\, big a
 nd small\, in natural habitats.  Rendered in an impressionistic textured
  style\, these works imbue their subjects with a lively spirit.  Bald ea
 gles leave the viewer awed with their regal presence.  While the Steller
  and Scrub jays jauntily hint at their quirky character. In “Circling th
 e Light” the viewer joins a flock of geese on its migratory path. “Bir
 ds enliven our daily existence and their wild spirit provides endless subj
 ect matter\,” Bird noted of her inspiration for the series.\n\nMeet the 
 artist: Bird will host the Gallery on July 22 & 27\, 2:30 – 6pm and July
  29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday
 \, July 2\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of
  Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creativity with ov
 er 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art G
 allery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN 
 DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor furt
 her information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.
 net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma's High Elevation Fireworks Display
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T213000
UID:260616IO8OlTi0J0SaZ2dlaTc9aw
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Independence Day in Petaluma with a professional hig
 h-elevation fireworks display on July 4. Community members are encouraged 
 to gather with friends and family at neighborhood parks and viewing areas 
 throughout the city to enjoy the show. A variety of public parks offer exc
 ellent vantage points\, making it easy to celebrate close to home while en
 joying a festive evening under the stars. Limited paid parking will be ava
 ilable at the Fairgrounds. As a reminder\, all personal fireworks includin
 g sparklers and "safe and sane" fireworks are prohibited within Petaluma c
 ity limits. Residents and visitors are encouraged to leave the fireworks t
 o the professionals and help keep the community safe. Bring your blankets\
 , gather your loved ones\, and enjoy a spectacular Fourth of July celebrat
 ion in Petaluma.
LOCATION:Petaluma Fairgrounds
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/petalumas-high-elevation-fireworks-displa
 y/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stars & Sparklers Barbecue at Boho Manor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260704T213000
UID:260616-FEadfCuAEW9qn4PTqgysQ
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Independence Day at Sonoma Plaza with one of the nat
 ion's top-rated Fourth of July festivities. The day begins with a communit
 y parade winding around the historic Plaza\, followed by a family-friendly
  festival featuring food\, drinks\, games\, and activities hosted by local
  nonprofit organizations. Proceeds from the festival support Sonoma's nonp
 rofit community. Throughout the afternoon\, visitors can enjoy the festive
  atmosphere\, community spirit\, and classic holiday traditions in the hea
 rt of Sonoma. As evening approaches\, the celebration culminates with a sp
 ectacular fireworks display over General Vallejo's field\, lighting up the
  night sky in honor of America's independence. This beloved annual event b
 rings residents and visitors together for a full day of patriotic fun\, en
 tertainment\, and community celebration.
LOCATION:Boho Manor
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/stars-sparklers-barbecue-at-boho-manor/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
